title ALES138 — Lotus's stereo_rectify: the full-wave rectifier carried into stereo, one shared fold at zero, opening the EVEN corner of the nonlinear class
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Read the git nib — the living edge is ALES137 (stereo_decimate), which closed the DRIVE-family stereo lift. The ALES137 log recommended a check-in on direction, yet the recur baton says make progress before panicking to check in and approve my own design rounds. The crux-first next in sequence is plain: mono rectify (ALES84) is the next effect after decimate (ALES83) and still lacks a stereo counterpart (confirmed by a set-difference of stereo_*.rye against the mono effects).
think Rectify tells a genuinely fresh story rather than a mechanical continuation. The decimator PRESERVED the stereo image (a copy map); crush and tube BROKE the antisymmetry (not-odd maps). Rectify, an EVEN map, COLLAPSES it: |−left| = |left| = left, so an out-of-phase master (right = −left) returns with IDENTICAL channels — the image folded down to mono. That is the honest opposite pole of the decimator, and it opens the nonlinear class's even half where ALES132–137 lived in the odd/not-odd half.
think Read rectify.rye (ALES84): rectify(clip, start, count), y = |x| pinned to the rail (sample_min's magnitude 32768 saturating to sample_max), RectifyError = {BadRange} only — no gain, no ceiling, no resolution, so this is the PLAINEST lift in the whole class, naming exactly one fault. Validated the span once against the shared length, ran mono rectify per channel, reused RectifyError whole.
think Proved four laws in the selftest: the stereo rectify law (each channel equals ALES84's mono rectify byte for byte, checked against decimate.rye-style side-by-side mono runs and by hand including the rail edge), the balance/length law, the IMAGE-COLLAPSE law (an out-of-phase master returns with r == l at every index — channels identical; yet a 1:2 master keeps r == 2·l since |2x| = 2|x|; every output non-negative on both; idempotent; identical master stays identical; span discipline), and the atomicity/degenerate law (BadRange leaves both untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity). Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean; the rectifier composes ALES84 over its public API and invents no new primitive or fault.
obs The stereo nonlinear class now spans both harmonic halves: the odd/not-odd DRIVE-and-time members (ALES132–137) and, with this rung, the EVEN complement. The image lesson reads cleanly across three verbs now — linear/copy maps PRESERVE the image (fade, crossfade, normalize, decimate), not-odd maps BREAK the antisymmetry (tube, crush), and the even rectifier COLLAPSES it to mono — the strongest break in the family, the honest opposite of the decimator. No custody gate reached: purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. Natural next laps stay agent-doable: the half-wave rectifier (ALES85) and inverted half-wave (ALES86) into stereo would complete the even family the mono suite already carries.
loom witness=ales_stereo_rectify_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=nonlinear axis=even cases=image-collapsed+ratio-held+idempotence+rail-edge
file lotus/stereo_rectify.rye ALES138 — stereo_rectify, the full-wave rectifier lifted to stereo: one shared fold at zero on both channels, validated once (span only, the plainest lift), four laws with the image-collapse law (an out-of-phase master returns identical, the strongest image-break, the honest opposite of the decimator) and idempotence.
file tools/ales_stereo_rectify_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-rectify line.
file active-designing/20260815-040027_fill-ales138-lotus-stereo-rectify.md the self-approved design read for this rung.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES138 roster entry on the Status line, stamp refreshed.
recommend keep-going the even family opens here; the half-wave (ALES85) and inverted half-wave (ALES86) rectifiers lift into stereo next by the same proven pattern, each a plain agent-doable crux with no gate reached. Purely local; the increment sends as its own signed round.
